  "_notes": [
    "game_state added locally, from a 4-player game driven through the cabinet's streamer.",
    "current_player and current_ball are adjacent in CPU RAM at 0x00032AB8 and 0x00032AB9, player low",
    "and ball high, the shape every Stern SAM game measured uses.",
    "Scores are 4 bytes on 4-byte centres from 0x021109E4. The sweep also offered 0x00036470 in CPU",
    "RAM, reading 251,000 / 250,500 / 250,500 / 251,500 -- four plausible, evenly spaced, monotonic",
    "values, and wrong. Scores are in NVRAM on every SAM game measured, which is what rejects it.",
    "player_count at 0x02110900, the one address every SAM game shares.",
    "Free Play measured directly: toggled in the operator menu with NVRAM captured either side. The",
    "value goes 1 -> 0 and its check byte 0xFE -> 0xFF, equal and opposite.",
    "It is one record of the 8-byte adjustment array at 0x02102008, where each record is a 32-bit",
    "little-endian value followed by a byte holding 0xFF minus the sum of the value's four bytes.",
    "Writing this field requires updating that check byte, or the game discards the change on reload."
  ]
